Mission sub-editor:
    Submission graph (graph PER mission, need a new datatable struct for this)
    - Double clicking a mission node should open an new tab which holds a graph for that mission

    - Sub-Mission graphs should NOT be able to edit transition rule 
        (Only Read-write in the Uber-Graph/Parent-Graph, read-only from the Sub-Mission graph)

    - Sub-Mission graphs should contain these elements:
        - Conversations and Characters 
            (A table of all characters which is read from to populate bindable characters). 			
            - Conversations may give/require Tags. Only sourced from tags defined in the mission entry, this can be modified in the Uber-Graph that contains said mission
            - A mission, must at the end of ALL possible ending paths supply needed Tags 
                (For example a mission may have 0-N amount of branching paths at the end
                Each path will have a required set of tags to end there, a terminating 
                                paths could have a universal END_MISSION tag, the other will be defined 
                                in the mission transition rules. So in a sub-mission graph we throw an 
                                error and don't allow compiling/saving unless all possible ends of a 
                                mission supply at-least on set of valid tags. This means that we will 
                                need to read this data from the mission table entry ad see which 
                                transitions it has.)


(Example graph)

	                        /[SUBOBECTIVE - TRIGGER::ITEM]>>>\
- [START - TRIGGER::CONVERSATION]> 				  -> [SUBOBECTIVE - TRIGGER::EVENT] 
	                        \[SUBOBECTIVE - TRIGGER::CHOICE]>/

-> [END[0] - SUPPLY TAGS VIA DROPDOWN LIST OF SETS]
-> [END[1] - SUPPLY TAGS VIA DROPDOWN LIST OF SETS]
-> [END[2] - SUPPLY TAGS VIA DROPDOWN LIST OF SETS]

Notes: 
    - END[N] limit is dictated by the amount of transition rules
    - Then furthermore, conversations has their own graphs, in the conversation system, so double clicking a conversation would open said graph

    - Items can have been picked up before reaching the trigger, in that case run a check when the subobjective enables to ensure that the player does now own or carry said item. 
        - Defined by ItemID, QoL selector that displays name & ID sourced from tables in the project. 
        - Whenever a new item is picked up check ID against active missions, and update accordingly.
        - Double clicking said item should just bring the user to the datatable where it is contained.

    - Choices needs to be source from the conversation graph to be read and serialized, and in can the conversation graph changes this need to force update the per-mission definitions, so they don't gor our of sync, 
        - Mimick the coreredirect stuff, make redirects in an ini, remap and updates a table if 
            mismatched choices are found and the redirects is valid. 
        - Maybe i'll code it such an ini is generated upon changes to choices names, and deletions 
        - and in case a deleted choice is reverted/undeleted, I revert/undelete the deletion-mapping

    - Events may be triggered from world-actions or actions in other missions (or latched to the tail-end of a mission). 
        - Events should have event-type IDs and maybe an event manager 
            - SWAPPABLE event managers with a shipped default, 
            - Allow projects to plug in their own event managers and event_ID interpreter, 
                - like predicate functionality. Need to think this through further..

